  witness_grip_obligations_are_derived_and_complete,
  witness_lift_qualification_refuses_on_axis_and_proof_load,
}

// One entry, one module-path index, seventeen claim bodies.
//
// MEASURED, not assumed. Running these as one process per witness cost 132-155 s each and about
// 37 minutes for the suite. A control run of a trivial 46-line entry against the same source root
// cost 133,171 ms, and the nine-witness public entry cost 146,352 ms, against 472 ms of logged
// compile phases. The tax is therefore FIXED and independent of what is being evaluated: roughly
// 133 s to build a module-path index over 2,141 .dag files and 24 MB before the entry graph
// narrows anything. Claim evaluation is the small remainder.
//
// "The witnesses take two minutes" was the wrong conclusion. The witnesses take milliseconds; the
// harness takes two minutes, and paying it once per witness multiplied it by seventeen. Reporting
// one wall-clock number per witness concealed an addressable harness defect as an inherent
// property of the claims -- the same shape as every other defect on this branch, where a number
// that looked like a measurement was never measuring what its name said.
data machine_tile_roster_cost_note: NonEmptyStr = "Fixed per-process index cost measured at ~133 s against 472 ms of logged compile phases; claim bodies are the small remainder. Seventeen separate invocations paid the index seventeen times."

type WitnessOutcome {
  name: NonEmptyStr
  passed: Bool
}

// Hand-listed and exact. A glob covers whatever happens to exist, so a witness deleted by an edit
// leaves the suite silently; a declared roster with an expected count reds instead.
data machine_tile_witness_outcomes: List<WitnessOutcome> = [
